1
00:00:04,567 --> 00:00:11,533
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,367
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:34,800
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,567 --> 00:00:40,667
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,533
[ENGINES REVVING]

6
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:44,700
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:45,833
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,433 --> 00:00:47,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:49,867 --> 00:00:50,900
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,200
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:54,933
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,433
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:57,567 --> 00:00:59,833
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:02,567
[ENGINES REVVING]

15
00:01:04,900 --> 00:01:06,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:08,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:09,833 --> 00:01:11,300
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,433 --> 00:01:12,567
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:13,733
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:23,033
<i>I'm sorry if you feel offended
that I'm proud of NLEA.</i>

21
00:01:23,167 --> 00:01:25,067
To improve NLEA's public image?

22
00:01:25,200 --> 00:01:27,667
Don't you think it'll be quicker
<i> if we both act on it?</i>

23
00:01:27,800 --> 00:01:29,933
<i> Once we see just one--</i>

24
00:01:30,067 --> 00:01:32,567
<i>My team will coordinate
with your team.</i>

25
00:01:32,700 --> 00:01:34,900
<i>If you find out anything
about the case, please...</i>

26
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,600
<i> let me know right away.</i>

27
00:01:36,733 --> 00:01:37,700
<i> You can count on me.</i>

28
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:39,133
<i> Dig into this!</i>

29
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:40,700
<i> For the sake of truth.</i>

30
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:43,033
No. For the sake of the ratings!

31
00:01:43,167 --> 00:01:44,133
<i>Since my brother is
not around, Ma...</i>

32
00:01:44,267 --> 00:01:46,300
<i> I'll finish what he started.</i>

33
00:01:46,433 --> 00:01:48,400
<i>We already had our revenge
on Samantha Jacinto.</i>

34
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:51,067
<i>My next target is the guy
he fought with in Chinatown.</i>

35
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:52,667
<i>I don't celebrate
birthdays anymore.</i>

36
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:55,567
<i>We'll work it out so we can
celebrate your birthday.</i>

37
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:57,567
<i> I need to find evidence.</i>

38
00:01:57,700 --> 00:01:59,100
<i>All I need is one piece
of evidence</i>

39
00:01:59,233 --> 00:02:03,533
<i>to prove Gabo has a connection
to the Zafras and Mr. Chan.</i>

40
00:02:06,033 --> 00:02:07,100
- Team.
- The boss is here.

41
00:02:07,233 --> 00:02:09,133
[GLOOMY MUSIC PLAYING]

42
00:02:09,267 --> 00:02:14,167
The NCIA and NLEA are conducting
a parallel investigation.

43
00:02:14,333 --> 00:02:16,467
Sir, those guys are arrogant.

44
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:17,633
That's right, sir.

45
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:19,033
They think they're all that.

46
00:02:19,167 --> 00:02:21,533
They're only trying
to boost NLEA's image,

47
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:23,100
that's why they're meddling.

48
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:25,700
But sir, why did you allow it?

49
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:29,433
Because I don't want
this NCIA issue

50
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:30,533
to be overshadowed by NLEA.

51
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:32,333
We'll only be criticized further

52
00:02:32,467 --> 00:02:34,033
If this blows up the media.

53
00:02:34,167 --> 00:02:36,667
it will create
a major distraction

54
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,767
from our investigation
and from finding Sam.

55
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:41,367
Sir Delgado's got a point.

56
00:02:42,033 --> 00:02:43,800
Let's just do this
for Ma'am Sam.

57
00:02:43,933 --> 00:02:46,767
[SEBASTIAN] But all findings
must go through me.

58
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,500
Because the moment
they don't comply,

59
00:02:48,667 --> 00:02:50,500
we'll stop cooperating
with them.

60
00:02:50,633 --> 00:02:53,533
Team, time is of the essence.

61
00:02:53,667 --> 00:02:55,567
As long as we haven't found Sam,

62
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:57,400
time is our enemy.

63
00:02:57,533 --> 00:03:00,700
So let's focus on finding her

64
00:03:00,833 --> 00:03:04,167
and those responsible for this.

65
00:03:04,467 --> 00:03:05,633
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

66
00:03:07,133 --> 00:03:09,200
[SEBASTIAN] Team, these
are our initial findings.

67
00:03:09,433 --> 00:03:10,833
Three of the five
deceased individuals

68
00:03:10,967 --> 00:03:12,567
remain unidentified.

69
00:03:12,700 --> 00:03:15,800
We ran facial recognition
and fingerprint checks,

70
00:03:15,933 --> 00:03:17,833
but unfortunately,
there were no matches.

71
00:03:17,967 --> 00:03:19,867
They don't exist
in our database.

72
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:22,100
Is it possible
they were hired guns?

73
00:03:22,267 --> 00:03:24,233
Not only that.
Next slide, please.

74
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:27,900
Ballistics recovered
multiple spent casings

75
00:03:28,033 --> 00:03:29,900
that do not appear
in our ballistic records.

76
00:03:30,033 --> 00:03:31,267
What about the weapons, sir?

77
00:03:31,400 --> 00:03:33,567
Of the weapons,
we recovered three.

78
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,467
Two had defaced serial numbers,

79
00:03:35,600 --> 00:03:37,600
while one was unregistered.

80
00:03:37,733 --> 00:03:38,900
In other words,

81
00:03:39,033 --> 00:03:40,767
we don't have a
definite identification

82
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:42,800
of the men Sam encountered.

83
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:45,367
Nor do we have a direct link
to the Zafras.

84
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:47,433
They really covered
their tracks.

85
00:03:48,167 --> 00:03:50,433
They made sure
they couldn't be identified.

86
00:03:50,867 --> 00:03:51,900
So team,

87
00:03:52,033 --> 00:03:54,800
until we can connect
one of these men to the Zafras,

88
00:03:54,967 --> 00:03:57,667
we won't be able to prove
that it was them

89
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,500
who ordered the ambush
on Sam.

90
00:03:59,633 --> 00:04:03,167
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

91
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,533
[MUSIC ENDS]

92
00:04:05,067 --> 00:04:07,767
[DEVICE POWERING UP]

93
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:10,267
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

94
00:04:10,400 --> 00:04:12,367
[DEVICE WHIRRING]

95
00:04:25,033 --> 00:04:32,033
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

96
00:04:33,933 --> 00:04:35,533
[RUDY] Thanks, Elton!
See you tomorrow!

97
00:04:36,833 --> 00:04:37,800
[SIGHS]

98
00:04:38,167 --> 00:04:43,633
[MUSIC BECOMES SUSPENSEFUL]

99
00:04:43,767 --> 00:04:45,233
[DRAWER SCRAPES]

100
00:04:46,033 --> 00:04:47,033
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

101
00:04:47,267 --> 00:04:48,967
You've all put me
in a tough spot.

102
00:04:49,100 --> 00:04:50,300
I didn't want to celebrate,

103
00:04:50,433 --> 00:04:51,633
and now I'm stuck.

104
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:54,033
[DANTE]
You're worrying over nothing.

105
00:04:54,267 --> 00:04:56,000
You won't have to spend
anything at all.

106
00:04:57,133 --> 00:04:58,267
That's right, Pa.

107
00:04:58,400 --> 00:04:59,967
Our neighbors offered to help.

108
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:03,567
We'll all pitch in so we can
celebrate your birthday.

109
00:05:04,133 --> 00:05:05,400
You know, son...

110
00:05:05,967 --> 00:05:07,367
I feel embarrassed.

111
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:08,933
I'm your father,

112
00:05:09,500 --> 00:05:11,800
yet you've become responsible
for me.

113
00:05:11,933 --> 00:05:14,167
Pa, don't think of it that way.

114
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:16,767
What matters is that
you're happy on your birthday.

115
00:05:16,900 --> 00:05:19,600
So tomorrow, I want you to wear
the clothes I bought you, okay?

116
00:05:19,733 --> 00:05:21,033
- I want you to look your best.
- [RUDY] Of course.

117
00:05:21,167 --> 00:05:22,567
- [CHUCKLES]
- That's a promise.

118
00:05:23,233 --> 00:05:24,900
- [SEBASTIAN] Sir.
- [DELGADO] Yes?

119
00:05:25,233 --> 00:05:26,067
[DOOR CLOSES]

120
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,433
May I suggest something?

121
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:28,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

122
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:30,433
Okay. Let me hear it.

123
00:05:30,567 --> 00:05:31,967
This is about Sam's case.

124
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:33,333
Okay, go on.

125
00:05:35,867 --> 00:05:37,167
I understand
we're now conducting

126
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,800
a parallel investigation
with NLEA.

127
00:05:38,933 --> 00:05:41,600
But it doesn't mean we have
to share everything with them.

128
00:05:41,733 --> 00:05:43,467
So, what is your suggestion?

129
00:05:43,867 --> 00:05:46,100
We don't need to disclose
all our information.

130
00:05:46,233 --> 00:05:49,300
Our intelligence
on the Zafras...

131
00:05:49,667 --> 00:05:50,967
should remain internal for now.

132
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,700
What if we need information
from them?

133
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:55,600
- They need to share it.
- [SCOFFS LIGHTLY]

134
00:05:55,733 --> 00:05:57,633
Tuazon, that's not coordination.

135
00:05:57,767 --> 00:05:58,767
That is control.

136
00:05:58,900 --> 00:06:00,000
Exactly, sir.

137
00:06:00,133 --> 00:06:01,700
And someone has to have it.

138
00:06:02,133 --> 00:06:03,267
And that's me.

139
00:06:03,667 --> 00:06:07,433
Because I report directly
to General Jacinto.

140
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,733
Do you have any other agendas?

141
00:06:09,867 --> 00:06:10,967
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

142
00:06:11,100 --> 00:06:12,167
What do you mean, sir?

143
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:13,467
I'm not blind.

144
00:06:14,167 --> 00:06:15,900
I know what is going on
in my agency.

145
00:06:16,033 --> 00:06:18,067
I know you like Sam.

146
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:20,600
And if that's the way to get--

147
00:06:20,733 --> 00:06:21,700
[SEBASTIAN] Sir.

148
00:06:22,067 --> 00:06:23,200
Sorry to interrupt.

149
00:06:23,333 --> 00:06:24,367
Sir, this is work.

150
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:27,500
And yes, Sam and I are
in a situationship.

151
00:06:27,633 --> 00:06:29,700
But... I want to help her.

152
00:06:30,567 --> 00:06:35,200
Wouldn't you want to know
who did this to her?

153
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:37,600
- Wouldn't you want to find her?
- [INHALES DEEPLY]

154
00:06:37,733 --> 00:06:38,833
[SEBASTIAN] Sir.

155
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:42,300
I'm protecting the NCIA.

156
00:06:42,733 --> 00:06:45,067
So I hope you don't put
any malice into this.

157
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,700
Okay, okay.

158
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,300
But...

159
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:51,133
If I see you getting too
personally involved

160
00:06:51,267 --> 00:06:54,167
in these matters,
I'll pull you out of the case.

161
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:55,633
- Understand?
- Yes, sir.

162
00:06:55,767 --> 00:06:56,867
Okay. Dismissed.

163
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:57,933
Thank you, sir.

164
00:06:58,067 --> 00:06:59,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

165
00:06:59,467 --> 00:07:01,300
You'll find out once
we're officially a couple, sir.

166
00:07:02,367 --> 00:07:04,400
[DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]

167
00:07:07,267 --> 00:07:08,733
Pa, excuse me.

168
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:10,767
- I'll just talk to the gang.
- [RUDY] Sure.

169
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:12,300
- Uncle.
- [DANTE] Go on.

170
00:07:12,433 --> 00:07:14,133
- Don't stay out too late.
- Yes, Pa.

171
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:15,567
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

172
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,333
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

173
00:07:17,467 --> 00:07:18,800
[DANTE] You know what, Rudy?

174
00:07:19,567 --> 00:07:21,333
You're very lucky
to have a son like him.

175
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:25,033
Even though he's reckless,
he has a good heart.

176
00:07:25,167 --> 00:07:28,300
Whatever shortcomings you have,
you're still his priority.

177
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:30,633
[RUDY] I know.

178
00:07:31,100 --> 00:07:33,100
That's why I feel so ashamed.

179
00:07:34,233 --> 00:07:36,967
I just hope someday
I'll get lucky,

180
00:07:37,100 --> 00:07:38,700
so I can make it up to him.

181
00:07:38,833 --> 00:07:39,867
[DANTE] Exactly.

182
00:07:40,300 --> 00:07:41,967
Don't lose hope.

183
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:43,600
Once your wound heals,

184
00:07:43,967 --> 00:07:45,667
you'll be the one to repay him.

185
00:07:46,033 --> 00:07:47,367
True. Come on, let's go inside.

186
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:48,467
- Let's go.
- Alright, alright.

187
00:07:48,633 --> 00:07:49,867
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:54,000
- [SCREEN DOOR OPENS, CLOSES]
- [INDISTINCT CHATTER]

189
00:07:54,967 --> 00:07:56,000
Hey.

190
00:07:56,300 --> 00:07:57,367
Where's Gabo?

191
00:07:57,800 --> 00:07:58,800
[RUDY] Uh...

192
00:07:58,933 --> 00:08:01,033
He's outside, chatting with Ipe.

193
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:02,500
- [DANTE MUMBLES]
- [GLASS THUDS]

194
00:08:03,833 --> 00:08:06,433
[DOG BARKING IN DISTANCE]

195
00:08:06,567 --> 00:08:13,533
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

196
00:08:21,633 --> 00:08:22,800
[ISOBEL] Max...

197
00:08:22,933 --> 00:08:24,333
Max, tell me.

198
00:08:24,467 --> 00:08:26,433
Is there any good news?

199
00:08:26,567 --> 00:08:32,333
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING]

200
00:08:32,467 --> 00:08:33,600
There's...

201
00:08:35,033 --> 00:08:36,733
no traces of Sam.

202
00:08:36,867 --> 00:08:38,900
I don't know what happened
to my sister.

203
00:08:39,033 --> 00:08:40,100
I don't know...

204
00:08:40,867 --> 00:08:43,000
where my sister is.

205
00:08:43,133 --> 00:08:45,600
You are just like your dad.

206
00:08:45,733 --> 00:08:47,300
You're all talk.

207
00:08:48,067 --> 00:08:51,533
Empty promises
of getting Sam home.

208
00:08:51,667 --> 00:08:54,500
You are not doing
your job enough!

209
00:08:55,667 --> 00:08:58,833
I'm exhausted, Ma.

210
00:09:01,300 --> 00:09:04,867
[SOBS] I've been looking
for my sister for days.

211
00:09:06,067 --> 00:09:07,433
Tell me.

212
00:09:07,567 --> 00:09:09,333
What did you do all day to help?

213
00:09:09,467 --> 00:09:11,367
All you do is worry and cry.

214
00:09:12,167 --> 00:09:13,333
Do you think that helps?

215
00:09:14,167 --> 00:09:15,733
Tell me,
do you think that helps?!

216
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,633
It doesn't!

217
00:09:22,367 --> 00:09:23,533
[MAX SIGHS]

218
00:09:26,367 --> 00:09:27,433
I'm sorry.

219
00:09:28,133 --> 00:09:29,167
You're right.

220
00:09:29,933 --> 00:09:30,767
[MAX SNIFFLES]

221
00:09:30,900 --> 00:09:32,500
You're saying

222
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:36,867
that I'm useless in this house.

223
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,167
Ma, that's not what I meant.

224
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:42,367
What are you fighting about?

225
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,500
Your daughter here
is just saying that,

226
00:09:49,633 --> 00:09:51,100
unlike her,

227
00:09:51,233 --> 00:09:54,300
I do nothing to help find Sam.

228
00:09:54,433 --> 00:09:55,700
[MAX SIGHS EXASPERATEDLY]

229
00:09:57,100 --> 00:09:58,367
Max has a point.

230
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,600
What have you done to help?

231
00:10:03,567 --> 00:10:04,600
What?

232
00:10:05,333 --> 00:10:06,400
[EXHALES]

233
00:10:07,833 --> 00:10:11,933
What can a civilian like me
do to help?

234
00:10:12,067 --> 00:10:13,600
Am I from NLEA?

235
00:10:14,933 --> 00:10:17,133
Do I have the resources
to investigate

236
00:10:17,267 --> 00:10:19,900
and find out the truth?!

237
00:10:20,033 --> 00:10:24,500
For all I know, you two
are keeping something from me.

238
00:10:24,633 --> 00:10:26,000
Especially you, Ricardo.

239
00:10:26,133 --> 00:10:27,500
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

240
00:10:29,467 --> 00:10:30,800
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

241
00:10:30,933 --> 00:10:34,700
I'm sorry, I think
I'm disturbing a family meeting.

242
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:36,133
It's okay. I'm willing to wait.

243
00:10:36,267 --> 00:10:37,233
I'll just stay here.

244
00:10:37,367 --> 00:10:39,033
- [MAX SIGHS]
- Sebastian.

245
00:10:39,167 --> 00:10:40,167
Auntie.

246
00:10:40,300 --> 00:10:43,333
Has the NCIA found Sam?

247
00:10:46,567 --> 00:10:48,067
Is it okay to butt in?

248
00:10:48,200 --> 00:10:50,733
- Are you guys done talking?
- Yeah.

249
00:10:50,867 --> 00:10:53,533
Auntie, actually...

250
00:10:55,767 --> 00:10:58,233
we're still actively
looking for her.

251
00:10:58,367 --> 00:10:59,567
[ISOBEL SIGHS]

252
00:11:02,067 --> 00:11:04,267
You're as bad as these two.

253
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,233
I'm starting to lose hope.

254
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:08,300
[ISOBEL HUFFS]

255
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:10,400
[FOOTSTEPS RETREATING]

256
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:14,200
Why are you here?

257
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,400
I'm here to offer my sympathies.

258
00:11:17,533 --> 00:11:21,100
And to update you on
NCIA's latest findings.

259
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,367
Honestly,

260
00:11:25,233 --> 00:11:27,200
I'm not impressed
by what your agency does.

261
00:11:27,333 --> 00:11:29,767
But whatever
information you have,

262
00:11:29,900 --> 00:11:31,500
I'll be willing to listen.

263
00:11:31,633 --> 00:11:33,367
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

264
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:35,967
- [BINOY] Is it this one?
- [TOLITS] Yes. That's the one.

265
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,467
[BINOY]
You're mine. You're mine, okay?

266
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:39,900
Gabo.

267
00:11:40,033 --> 00:11:41,200
What's up?

268
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:43,700
Did you spot any outsiders?

269
00:11:43,833 --> 00:11:44,800
No.

270
00:11:44,933 --> 00:11:47,500
We've been here for a while.
No one suspicious.

271
00:11:47,633 --> 00:11:50,733
Gabo, I think people are scared
to come here in Paradise.

272
00:11:50,867 --> 00:11:53,633
You were aggressive
and pointing at them last time.

273
00:11:53,767 --> 00:11:55,300
For sure, they got terrified.

274
00:11:56,033 --> 00:11:57,333
They wouldn't dare return.

275
00:11:57,467 --> 00:12:00,100
I've asked some men
to watch the streets.

276
00:12:00,233 --> 00:12:02,467
If they come back,
they'll inform us right away.

277
00:12:03,133 --> 00:12:04,900
Gabo, I'm hungry.

278
00:12:05,033 --> 00:12:06,600
Chips won't do it.

279
00:12:06,733 --> 00:12:08,733
I think
it just made me hungrier.

280
00:12:08,867 --> 00:12:10,033
Let's get out of here.

281
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:12,900
I don't think
anyone would dare show up.

282
00:12:13,033 --> 00:12:16,833
And you said you've asked
people to guard the alleys.

283
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,367
Come on. Food and drinks on me.

284
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:22,433
- Nice!
- Nice!

285
00:12:22,567 --> 00:12:24,433
- Thank you, Gabo!
- Thank you!

286
00:12:24,567 --> 00:12:26,167
Keep pushing!
Attack! Attack! Attack!

287
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:27,867
- Frisky! Frisky!
- [WOMAN] It's open 24 hours.

288
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,967
[ROUSING MUSIC PLAYING]

289
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,733
[WOMAN] Aw, thank you, baby!

290
00:12:31,867 --> 00:12:33,333
- Miss?
- [BOY] Keep going!

291
00:12:33,467 --> 00:12:35,133
Yes, yes, yes.
I love you so much.

292
00:12:35,267 --> 00:12:36,333
I love you, baby...

293
00:12:36,467 --> 00:12:37,567
Miss.

294
00:12:39,067 --> 00:12:42,067
Of course. Yes, I'm here.

295
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,433
I'm in my computer shop.

296
00:12:43,567 --> 00:12:45,233
Yes, yes. I'm waiting.

297
00:12:45,367 --> 00:12:48,133
- Yes. I love you so much.
- [MAN] Go on!

298
00:12:50,433 --> 00:12:51,667
Kill it! Kill it!

299
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:54,167
- Mister?
- Why?

300
00:12:54,300 --> 00:12:55,667
I'm sorry for this.

301
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:58,167
I badly need
to use the computer.

302
00:12:58,300 --> 00:13:01,000
Do you have any spare coins?

303
00:13:01,133 --> 00:13:02,267
I do.

304
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:06,267
- Oh, thank you.
- It's all good.

305
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,100
[COIN CLINKS]

306
00:13:09,233 --> 00:13:10,800
You can use it now, miss.

307
00:13:10,933 --> 00:13:12,467
- Thank you.
- Okay.

308
00:13:22,367 --> 00:13:24,400
Miss Simang,
can we get beers, please?

309
00:13:24,533 --> 00:13:26,900
- There we go.
- Okay.

310
00:13:27,033 --> 00:13:29,067
Six glasses
and six grilled intestines.

311
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:31,300
- Freezing cold beers, please.
- Make it extra charred!

312
00:13:31,433 --> 00:13:32,600
[SIMANG] On it.

313
00:13:34,067 --> 00:13:35,033
Oh.

314
00:13:35,733 --> 00:13:36,700
Where's Tekla?

315
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:39,833
Oh, Gabo.
Jealousy is eating her up.

316
00:13:39,967 --> 00:13:42,200
She was so drunk
before she went home.

317
00:13:42,333 --> 00:13:44,633
Truth is, Gabo,
she's really hurt.

318
00:13:44,767 --> 00:13:46,133
She's in love with you.

319
00:13:46,267 --> 00:13:48,800
I've told her she wouldn't
stand a chance with you.

320
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:50,100
But she's stubborn.

321
00:13:50,233 --> 00:13:51,700
I told her
just to pick me instead.

322
00:13:51,833 --> 00:13:54,533
Saying that to her
only hurt her more.

323
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,933
Imagine she agrees to marry you.

324
00:13:57,067 --> 00:13:58,933
She wakes up every morning
seeing your face.

325
00:13:59,067 --> 00:14:01,433
That's as good as punching her.

326
00:14:01,567 --> 00:14:03,033
Hey, watch your words.

327
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:09,067
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

328
00:14:09,200 --> 00:14:11,967
[SAM]<i> I can't access
</i> NCIA's database here.

329
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:14,933
<i>They'll be able to trace it
right away.</i>

330
00:14:16,067 --> 00:14:19,567
<i> I should only look for
</i>publicly available information.

331
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:21,033
<i> That would be more discreet.</i>

332
00:14:22,800 --> 00:14:25,333
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

333
00:14:27,367 --> 00:14:30,267
<i>Maybe I can find
Gabo's case file here.</i>

334
00:14:31,333 --> 00:14:34,600
<i>If so, I'd be able to see
the people involved.</i>

335
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,567
[WHISPERS] Samantha.

336
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:43,200
"Gabriel Magtibay
Case No. 18-04567"

337
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,700
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

338
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:55,200
<i> The victim was a congressman?</i>

339
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:58,200
<i> Why was he killed?</i>

340
00:15:00,700 --> 00:15:01,767
Uh, Gabo.

341
00:15:02,433 --> 00:15:04,500
Do you think Gloria
will stay here for a while?

342
00:15:05,733 --> 00:15:09,400
I'm just worried
her team blindsides us.

343
00:15:10,267 --> 00:15:13,800
He brought it up again!
I'm riled up! I'm all riled up!

344
00:15:13,933 --> 00:15:16,600
They beat us up, Gabo!

345
00:15:16,733 --> 00:15:20,900
They dare come here
and I'll smash their faces.

346
00:15:21,033 --> 00:15:24,067
I'll do exactly
what they did to us!

347
00:15:24,200 --> 00:15:26,533
Those animals.
I haven't gotten my revenge.

348
00:15:26,667 --> 00:15:29,133
They'll get a taste
of Ginintuang Lupa's wrath.

349
00:15:29,267 --> 00:15:30,300
Just wait and see. Argh!

350
00:15:30,433 --> 00:15:32,733
Here we go again.
Acting all cocky.

351
00:15:32,867 --> 00:15:35,300
When a real fight happens,
you all fold.

352
00:15:35,467 --> 00:15:37,133
Enough with the fights, please.

353
00:15:38,867 --> 00:15:40,467
Let's stay away from trouble.

354
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:44,633
Let's prioritize
keeping Gloria safe.

355
00:15:44,767 --> 00:15:46,667
And how to keep her enemies
from tracking her down here.

356
00:15:48,167 --> 00:15:49,633
Don't worry, Gabo.

357
00:15:49,767 --> 00:15:51,833
One word from you
and we'll do it.

358
00:15:51,967 --> 00:15:53,467
Just look after Gloria.

359
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:57,167
If her memory comes back,
that's definitely trouble.

360
00:15:59,567 --> 00:16:01,733
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

361
00:16:03,067 --> 00:16:04,833
[SAM] There are no more records?

362
00:16:04,967 --> 00:16:07,067
<i> The main case file isn't here.</i>

363
00:16:09,600 --> 00:16:13,400
[KEYBOARD CLACKING]

364
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,667
<i> Gold smuggling.</i>

365
00:16:26,900 --> 00:16:28,067
That's what
I'm worried about, Gabo.

366
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:30,567
When Gloria's memory comes back,

367
00:16:30,700 --> 00:16:32,067
she'll get mad at you.

368
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,333
She'll hate you.

369
00:16:34,100 --> 00:16:37,600
Once she finds out that
we've been feeding her lies,

370
00:16:37,733 --> 00:16:38,900
despite helping her,

371
00:16:39,033 --> 00:16:40,367
in the end,
you'll still be the bad guy.

372
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,400
- [BONG] Mm-hmm.
- [IPE] You're in the wrong.

373
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:53,400
<i>Just a few days after
the gold smuggling issue,</i>

374
00:16:53,533 --> 00:16:55,100
<i> he was immediately killed.</i>

375
00:16:55,233 --> 00:16:57,333
For what reason? To silence him?

376
00:16:58,233 --> 00:17:00,400
<i>The Tiger runs
the gold smuggling</i>

377
00:17:00,533 --> 00:17:01,733
<i> in the Philippines.</i>

378
00:17:02,733 --> 00:17:05,767
<i>Do Zafras kill people
before they can rat them out?</i>

379
00:17:06,467 --> 00:17:09,100
<i>But why hasn't he taken me
to the Zafras?</i>

380
00:17:09,233 --> 00:17:11,300
<i>Is it to get even?
Did he leave the group?</i>

381
00:17:11,433 --> 00:17:14,333
<i>Or he's holding me hostage
to piss off the Zafras?</i>

382
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,733
<i> If he knows who I am,</i>

383
00:17:15,867 --> 00:17:18,633
<i>he can use me
against the Zafras.</i>

384
00:17:18,767 --> 00:17:21,833
<i>Or maybe he'll use me
to get ransom from the Zafras?</i>

385
00:17:22,367 --> 00:17:24,733
I can only imagine
what you're going through.

386
00:17:24,733 --> 00:17:27,967
I'm only somewhat close
with Sam,

387
00:17:27,967 --> 00:17:29,967
but I'm really worried.

388
00:17:29,967 --> 00:17:32,633
What more with you
when you're her family?

389
00:17:32,633 --> 00:17:36,233
I just want to let you know
that I am here for you.

390
00:17:36,233 --> 00:17:37,900
Because you're like family
to me!

391
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:40,533
So your worries
are also my worries.

392
00:17:42,533 --> 00:17:44,633
What I want to hear
is your investigation.

393
00:17:44,633 --> 00:17:47,133
Oh, yes, sir.
You came to the office, right?

394
00:17:47,133 --> 00:17:48,900
We already told you everything.

395
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:52,367
At this point, we're still
gathering information.

396
00:17:52,367 --> 00:17:54,067
- Until now?
- Oh, yes.

397
00:17:54,067 --> 00:17:55,800
More information at this point.

398
00:17:56,333 --> 00:18:00,133
With NCIA, you really have
a lot of research, analysis,

399
00:18:00,133 --> 00:18:02,867
- paperwork, and rituals!
- [SEBASTIAN CHUCKLES]

400
00:18:02,867 --> 00:18:05,633
Max, you get it!
That's our expertise.

401
00:18:05,633 --> 00:18:08,200
It takes so many rituals
before you start moving!

402
00:18:08,800 --> 00:18:11,533
Dad, NLEA's already covered
so many areas.

403
00:18:11,533 --> 00:18:13,867
We've already asked
so many people.

404
00:18:13,867 --> 00:18:15,267
Wait a minute, Max.

405
00:18:15,267 --> 00:18:16,267
[SEBASTIAN INHALES DEEPLY]

406
00:18:17,300 --> 00:18:18,667
Are you saying

407
00:18:18,667 --> 00:18:22,000
that NCIA is moving slow
compared to NLEA?

408
00:18:22,033 --> 00:18:25,067
Not just compared to NLEA.
In general, you do move slow.

409
00:18:25,067 --> 00:18:27,467
That's what you think,
but the truth is,

410
00:18:27,467 --> 00:18:29,400
I've already sent out teams

411
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:32,767
to the nearby villages
near Soriano Street.

412
00:18:32,767 --> 00:18:35,733
To gather more and more
and more information?

413
00:18:35,733 --> 00:18:36,800
Oh, yes!

414
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:39,500
A lot of eyes and ears
are connected to this.

415
00:18:39,500 --> 00:18:42,200
I mean,
in a situation like this,

416
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:45,233
all of your actions
should be calculated.

417
00:18:45,233 --> 00:18:47,400
You have to be disciplined,
you know?

418
00:18:47,400 --> 00:18:49,333
You have to be smart.

419
00:18:49,333 --> 00:18:52,767
You didn't ask,
but I'll tell you this.

420
00:18:52,767 --> 00:18:55,033
I graduated cum laude
in my undergrad university.

421
00:18:56,033 --> 00:18:57,233
See, sir?

422
00:18:58,900 --> 00:19:02,433
So I know
that what I'm doing will work.

423
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:05,233
I thought you went here
to check on us,

424
00:19:05,233 --> 00:19:06,533
and to give us updates.

425
00:19:06,533 --> 00:19:09,033
But all you've done
is show off!

426
00:19:09,033 --> 00:19:10,767
I don't have to do that.

427
00:19:10,767 --> 00:19:12,833
With a face like mine?
Come on.

428
00:19:13,733 --> 00:19:17,567
You don't need
to impress us, okay?

429
00:19:18,100 --> 00:19:20,900
Sebastian, just come back
when you have solid information.

430
00:19:20,900 --> 00:19:22,800
Of course, sir.
You can count on that.

431
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,567
Next time, there will be
more information.

432
00:19:26,267 --> 00:19:28,000
And I'll tell you
my theory, sir.

433
00:19:29,167 --> 00:19:30,167
[MAX SCOFFS]

434
00:19:39,433 --> 00:19:40,433
Oh, it's nighttime.

435
00:19:41,667 --> 00:19:43,533
It's getting late.
I should go.

436
00:19:43,533 --> 00:19:44,833
I'll find my way out.

437
00:19:44,833 --> 00:19:45,833
Thank you!

438
00:19:47,467 --> 00:19:48,433
Bye.

439
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:52,767
Wow. Dad!

440
00:19:53,900 --> 00:19:55,200
Do you really think
their investigation

441
00:19:55,200 --> 00:19:56,333
will actually lead anywhere?

442
00:19:56,867 --> 00:19:58,233
I don't know, Max.

443
00:19:58,233 --> 00:19:59,633
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

444
00:19:59,633 --> 00:20:00,800
But at this point...

445
00:20:02,300 --> 00:20:05,167
whatever help anyone can give...

446
00:20:06,333 --> 00:20:07,567
I'll take it.

447
00:20:08,867 --> 00:20:12,833
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

448
00:20:12,833 --> 00:20:14,733
I'm worrying about tomorrow.

449
00:20:17,233 --> 00:20:18,567
It's Papa's birthday tomorrow.

450
00:20:19,567 --> 00:20:23,033
I'm sure Auntie Betchay
will be there the whole day.

451
00:20:23,033 --> 00:20:24,333
I can't help but worry.

452
00:20:25,333 --> 00:20:27,167
What if she sees Gloria?

453
00:20:27,167 --> 00:20:30,200
Once Miss Betchay finds out,
we're all dead.

454
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:31,867
We know how Miss Betchay is.

455
00:20:31,867 --> 00:20:33,433
I'm sure she'll tell everyone
about it.

456
00:20:33,433 --> 00:20:35,100
- Yeah.
- It'll be a mess!

457
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:37,333
Whatever happens, happens.

458
00:20:37,333 --> 00:20:39,167
I just hope that if
Auntie Betchay does see her...

459
00:20:39,867 --> 00:20:42,033
I can at least explain
why Gloria's here.

460
00:20:42,667 --> 00:20:45,233
And I hope she doesn't speak
harshly to Gloria.

461
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:47,033
Who knows,
she might ask Gloria to leave.

462
00:20:47,033 --> 00:20:49,600
You walked into
a very difficult problem, Gabo.

463
00:20:49,600 --> 00:20:51,733
It's a lot harder
than all our problems!

464
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:53,867
There's nothing I can do.

465
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:59,267
I have to save Gloria.
Her life is in danger.

466
00:20:59,267 --> 00:21:03,633
And the people looking for her
all want to kill her.

467
00:21:03,633 --> 00:21:07,000
Our community
is the safest place for her.

468
00:21:08,700 --> 00:21:11,667
- [MAN 1] Hey, Caloy!
- [MAN 2] Man, they're pretty!

469
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:14,467
- They're all young and fresh!
- She looks pretty!

470
00:21:14,467 --> 00:21:16,567
So did you wear a lot
of makeup?

471
00:21:16,567 --> 00:21:18,200
- Yes.
- Of course.

472
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:20,900
- Look.
- Let me see. There.

473
00:21:20,900 --> 00:21:23,033
Did you spray perfume?

474
00:21:23,033 --> 00:21:24,967
Did your brush your teeth?
Did you?

475
00:21:24,967 --> 00:21:26,700
- Hey! Did you?
- Yes!

476
00:21:26,700 --> 00:21:28,800
- You brushed your teeth?
- I did!

477
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:30,400
- Boyet, get ready.
- [BOYET] Yes.

478
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:34,067
When I say open,
switch the lights on.

479
00:21:34,067 --> 00:21:41,100
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

480
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:43,167
Alright, alright,
I'll go with her.

481
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:47,900
- Oh! I know who you want!
- Betchay!

482
00:21:47,900 --> 00:21:49,967
- Yes.
- It's a regular, right?

483
00:21:49,967 --> 00:21:52,067
Aya, Aya. Aya.

484
00:21:52,067 --> 00:21:54,367
- Oh! Kulas! My god!
- Hello!

485
00:21:54,367 --> 00:21:57,567
Alright. Come inside,
go take a seat.

486
00:21:57,567 --> 00:21:59,000
[AYA] Let's sit here!

487
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:03,967
[BETCHAY] Girls, are you ready?
When I tell you to face front--

488
00:22:03,967 --> 00:22:09,200
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

489
00:22:09,200 --> 00:22:12,633
Hello! Come inside, come inside!

490
00:22:12,633 --> 00:22:14,333
Oh, that's who you want?

491
00:22:14,333 --> 00:22:16,433
Wait, line up for now
so we have some order.

492
00:22:16,467 --> 00:22:17,867
They're here.

493
00:22:17,867 --> 00:22:21,467
I'll show you my girls!

494
00:22:21,467 --> 00:22:23,367
Ready, switch the lights on!

495
00:22:24,233 --> 00:22:27,067
Face front! Smoke!

496
00:22:27,833 --> 00:22:31,933
First off is Diana!

497
00:22:31,933 --> 00:22:33,100
[BETCHAY CACKLES]

498
00:22:33,100 --> 00:22:36,433
That's Diana! It's her.
She's Diana.

499
00:22:36,433 --> 00:22:39,333
See, it looks just like her!
Okay, who's next?

500
00:22:40,600 --> 00:22:45,800
Joyce! Joyce is still very sexy!
Go with her to your table!

501
00:22:45,800 --> 00:22:49,200
Oh, you want our brown beauty!

502
00:22:49,233 --> 00:22:53,000
Oh, Priscilla.
Here, this is her.

503
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,267
Go sit over there.

504
00:22:54,267 --> 00:22:56,200
Last but not the least,

505
00:22:56,200 --> 00:23:01,167
the most beautiful
and the sexiest,

506
00:23:01,167 --> 00:23:04,367
it's Rosanna! Hey, smile!

507
00:23:04,367 --> 00:23:07,867
- Hello!
- Table, table. Go!

508
00:23:07,867 --> 00:23:12,233
Hey, give them the menu! Hurry!

509
00:23:12,233 --> 00:23:17,500
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

510
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:19,533
[DIDAY] Kulas! Kulas!

511
00:23:21,800 --> 00:23:24,700
Kulas! Nikolas, where are you?!

512
00:23:24,700 --> 00:23:28,033
- Ma, why are you screaming?
- Your father disappeared!

513
00:23:28,033 --> 00:23:29,967
He's probably drinking
with Mister Kanor.

514
00:23:29,967 --> 00:23:31,033
Leave them alone.

515
00:23:31,033 --> 00:23:33,833
Get my bolo!
I'll chop your father up!

516
00:23:33,833 --> 00:23:35,767
- Ma, just let him!
- We'll find him!

517
00:23:35,767 --> 00:23:37,733
- Just leave it.
- Hurry up!

518
00:23:37,733 --> 00:23:39,433
Where's the bolo?

519
00:23:39,433 --> 00:23:41,100
Look over there! Find it!

520
00:23:41,633 --> 00:23:42,833
Ma, this is crazy!

521
00:23:43,133 --> 00:23:44,833
You guys take care
of Tekla, okay?

522
00:23:45,667 --> 00:23:46,833
Talk to her.

523
00:23:47,367 --> 00:23:48,833
Knock some sense into her.

524
00:23:48,833 --> 00:23:50,633
Who knows what she might do
to Gloria.

525
00:23:51,333 --> 00:23:52,900
[IPE] We've got Tekla, Gabo.

526
00:23:54,333 --> 00:23:55,467
Come on.

527
00:23:56,133 --> 00:23:58,233
I'm going to bed. Gloria's
probably waiting for me.

528
00:23:58,233 --> 00:23:59,333
[EVERYONE CHUCKLES]

529
00:23:59,333 --> 00:24:00,800
Wait...

530
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:02,333
- Whoa!
- [CHUCKLING]

531
00:24:02,333 --> 00:24:05,467
Gabo, you know
what's the best feeling of all?

532
00:24:05,667 --> 00:24:06,900
Having someone waiting for you.

533
00:24:06,900 --> 00:24:08,067
[IPE CLAPS]

534
00:24:08,067 --> 00:24:11,867
And the best part, Gabo,
is what happens next.

535
00:24:11,867 --> 00:24:13,800
Are you going to be together
in the bedroom?

536
00:24:13,800 --> 00:24:15,067
Sleeping side by side?

537
00:24:15,067 --> 00:24:17,067
- Hey!
- Gabo!

538
00:24:17,067 --> 00:24:19,000
Gabo, are you sleeping
next to her?

539
00:24:19,000 --> 00:24:20,967
Are you two going to be
all cuddled up?

540
00:24:20,967 --> 00:24:23,733
[OVERLAPPING GIGGLES]

541
00:24:23,733 --> 00:24:26,567
Gabo, no matter what happens...

542
00:24:27,667 --> 00:24:30,167
- Take a shower first, okay?
- [DABOY CHUCKLING]

543
00:24:30,200 --> 00:24:33,033
Then brush your teeth
and put on some cologne.

544
00:24:33,033 --> 00:24:35,733
[BINOY] And don't embarrass
Ginintuang Lupa.

545
00:24:35,733 --> 00:24:37,800
- Show her what we're made of.
- [GABO] Fine!

546
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:38,933
Go home, all of you.

547
00:24:38,933 --> 00:24:40,700
- There you go!
- Let's go, guys.

548
00:24:40,700 --> 00:24:42,100
Why are you in such a hurry?

549
00:24:42,100 --> 00:24:43,767
[LAUGHTER]

550
00:24:43,767 --> 00:24:45,067
[GABO CHUCKLING]

551
00:24:45,067 --> 00:24:47,733
[CHAOTIC CHATTER]

552
00:24:47,733 --> 00:24:49,567
[IPE] I don't want to drink
anymore!

553
00:24:51,933 --> 00:24:58,833
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

554
00:25:02,733 --> 00:25:05,100
[GABO] They're trying
to get me to be like them.

555
00:25:14,733 --> 00:25:21,567
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

556
00:25:36,767 --> 00:25:43,600
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

557
00:25:45,767 --> 00:25:46,833
Lord...

558
00:25:51,200 --> 00:25:53,033
please forgive me.

559
00:25:55,233 --> 00:25:57,700
[GABO] I'm only a man.

560
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:03,567
If I happen to make
a mistake and sin...

561
00:26:05,767 --> 00:26:08,133
I swear I don't mean to.

562
00:26:09,100 --> 00:26:15,200
And if something unexpected
does happen,

563
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:20,033
please let her be the one
to start it.

564
00:26:20,667 --> 00:26:22,900
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

565
00:26:22,900 --> 00:26:25,100
Please take care of me, Lord.

566
00:26:26,567 --> 00:26:27,633
Amen.

567
00:26:29,667 --> 00:26:35,067
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

568
00:26:35,067 --> 00:26:36,767
I need to take care
of my breath.

569
00:26:36,767 --> 00:26:38,067
[SNIFFS]

570
00:26:39,067 --> 00:26:40,933
I'm getting
a little stinky, too.

571
00:26:43,367 --> 00:26:44,933
Don't worry, Love.

572
00:26:46,333 --> 00:26:48,433
I'll be ready for you.

573
00:26:48,433 --> 00:26:50,000
I'll put on some cologne.

574
00:26:52,267 --> 00:26:54,200
I'll scrub off all this grime.

575
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,567
Because I want...

576
00:26:58,767 --> 00:27:01,000
when we sleep beside
each other...

577
00:27:02,600 --> 00:27:06,500
for you to be the one
to hug me and kiss me.

578
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,500
I'll be back!

579
00:27:10,867 --> 00:27:17,700
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

580
00:27:21,133 --> 00:27:28,167
[MUSIC BECOMES PENSIVE]

581
00:27:35,467 --> 00:27:41,833
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

582
00:27:43,767 --> 00:27:45,467
[MISCHIEVOUS LAUGH]

583
00:27:46,267 --> 00:27:48,067
I've waited so long for this.

584
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:55,633
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

585
00:27:56,233 --> 00:27:58,600
I've suffered in prison
for so long.

586
00:28:00,700 --> 00:28:01,800
My love!

587
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:02,967
[HUFFS]

588
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:06,333
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

589
00:28:06,467 --> 00:28:08,367
[SNIFFS] Mmh!

590
00:28:08,500 --> 00:28:09,767
It's kicking!

591
00:28:10,500 --> 00:28:13,967
I'll just take a shower
and then...

592
00:28:14,100 --> 00:28:15,000
[CHUCKLES]

593
00:28:15,133 --> 00:28:17,000
...let's get it on.

594
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:26,367
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

595
00:28:33,633 --> 00:28:36,000
Soap, soap, soap...

596
00:28:36,133 --> 00:28:38,200
to make me smell good.

597
00:28:38,333 --> 00:28:43,400
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

598
00:28:46,467 --> 00:28:48,600
To freshen my breath!

599
00:28:48,733 --> 00:28:53,033
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

600
00:28:53,533 --> 00:28:55,500
Time for a bath!

601
00:28:56,667 --> 00:29:00,367
Come on, baby,
take a shower!

602
00:29:00,500 --> 00:29:01,567
Yeah!

603
00:29:01,700 --> 00:29:07,833
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

604
00:29:08,567 --> 00:29:10,867
[QUIRKY MUSIC CONTINUES]

605
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:14,767
My love, get ready.

606
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:17,033
The lion's getting really angry.

607
00:29:18,667 --> 00:29:19,733
[GROWLS]

608
00:29:20,667 --> 00:29:22,033
This Friday...

609
00:29:22,167 --> 00:29:24,633
<i>We have to do our best
because my future in-laws</i>

610
00:29:24,767 --> 00:29:26,033
<i> are really counting on me.</i>

611
00:29:26,167 --> 00:29:27,933
<i>Victor Zafra's father
used to be a cop.</i>

612
00:29:28,067 --> 00:29:31,233
<i>He was kicked off the force
for misconduct.</i>

613
00:29:31,400 --> 00:29:32,900
<i> Raid their businesses.</i>

614
00:29:33,033 --> 00:29:34,567
<i>He's getting back at you
through Sam?</i>

615
00:29:34,700 --> 00:29:36,567
<i>I'm sure we need to put
pressure on him</i>

616
00:29:36,700 --> 00:29:37,967
<i> so he can't make a move.</i>

617
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:39,533
<i> This is a raid! Get down!</i>

618
00:29:40,233 --> 00:29:42,033
<i>- Who's that?
- [GROWLS]</i>

619
00:29:42,467 --> 00:29:43,367
<i> I'm a lion!</i>

620
00:29:43,500 --> 00:29:44,767
<i> What lion?</i>

621
00:29:44,900 --> 00:29:47,167
<i>Didn't you say that
you wanted us to make a baby?</i>

622
00:29:47,300 --> 00:29:50,467
<i>The lion and the tiger
are about to get it on.</i>
